Provides: g15-fanctl-daemon, g15-fanctl-cli, g15-fanctl-gui
Description: Fan/thermal monitoring and control for Dell G-series gaming laptops
 Unified package (daemon + CLI + GTK4 GUI) for monitoring and controlling
 fan/thermal behavior on Dell G-series gaming laptops (G15/G16 family),
 covering Intel 11th-13th gen H/HX CPUs (including the Core i5-13500HX
 class) and NVIDIA RTX 20/30/40-series mobile GPUs.
 .
 Includes:
  * g15-fancontrold - systemd service reading CPU/GPU temperature, fan RPM,
    and utilization from documented Linux hwmon/ACPI interfaces, and (where
    firmware supports it) applying thermal profiles and manual fan curves
    via the kernel's platform_profile and dell_smm_hwmon interfaces. Exposes
    a D-Bus API at org.g15fanctl.Daemon.
  * g15fanctl - scriptable CLI client, plus standalone hardware detection
    that works without the daemon running.
  * g15-fanctl-gui - GTK4/Libadwaita dashboard, fan control, thermal
    profile, and custom fan curve GUI, with live graphs, notifications,
    and system tray integration.
 .
 On hardware where dell_smm_hwmon or platform_profile aren't available, the
 app automatically falls back to monitoring-only mode rather than guessing;
 see /usr/share/doc/g15-fanctl/ for the full hardware compatibility notes.
 .
 This package does not install or manage the NVIDIA driver itself. GPU
 telemetry uses whatever NVIDIA driver is already on the system (via
 nvidia-smi) and is simply omitted if none is installed. Manage your NVIDIA
 driver the normal way (Software & Updates' Additional Drivers tab, or
 `ubuntu-drivers autoinstall`) rather than through this package.
